== Multiple levels of communication
- One-to-many
  - Mass communication
  - Public communication to an audience
- Many-to-many
  - Group communication
- One-to-one
  - Interpersonal communication
- In your head
  - Intrapersonal communication

= How do we speak
- Speaking takes up to 5 times longer to generate a work compared to recognizing it
- Speaking always requires intention (working memory & system 2 thinking)
- Word recognition becomes often automatic
- Writing is also typically intentional

== Speaking stages
1. Conceptualization
   - interface between thinking and language production
2. Formulation
   - propositions and concepts are represented as lemmas or lexical entries
3. Phonological encoding
   - the lemmas are encoded in actual grammatical structure
4. articulation
   - muscles are activated and speaking occurs

Because of all this (very exhausting), speech is shortened alot and contextualized to save energy

= Language and social context
Central for successful communication: a common ground in the respective context
- Shared beliefs
- Shared assumptions
- Shared Knowledge #emoji.face.nerd

Good cominicators would estimate these correctly and they adapt to it 

Common ground emerges from two sources:
- Communal common ground (= community/ culture based)
- Personal common ground (= participants shared experiences)

