== Computer-mediated communication
Can differ from face-to-face communication
- Synchronicity
• Permanency
• Anonymity
• Less cues (e.g., lack of nonverbal communication)
• Other cues (e.g., emojis)

== Media richness theory
Basic idea: Match the richness of the chosen communication medium to the significance of reducing uncertainty and establishing equivocality
- Richness
  - immediate feedback, multiple cues, language variety, personal focus

= The Social Identity Deindividuation Effects Model (SIDE)
- In anonymous digital contexts, our personal identity is less important
- Instead: Stronger orientation towards the norms in the respective digital context
  - We adapt to the norms of communication
- If the norms are hostile: More hostile behaviour
- If the norms are constructive: More constructive behaviour